  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">DEC Middle East Appeal 2024 Phase 1</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Oxfam and PDWSA seeks to address the urgent food security and basic needs of communities in Gaza to ensure that the most vulnerable, crisis-affected individuals are supported with life-saving humanitarian assistance through improved food security.  In Gaza, underphase 1 of DEC, Oxfam and local partner will target 1900 of the most vulnerable displaced people living in informal shelters with emergency multi purpose cash assistance and protection services
Oxfam has been present in the OPT since the 1950s,with a country office established in the 1980s. Registered in country, Oxfam operates humanitarian and development interventions in the West Bank and Gaza through 70 staff members across offices in Ramallah, Gaza City, and Jerusalem. Approximately 30 Gaza-based staff are directly involved in implementing responses with support from a team of 10 staff in Jerusalem and others in Jordan and Egypt to manage coordination. The response in Gaza is led by the Response Lead, Gaza Programme lead and the team in Gaza with full functions (programme, support and management) to coordinate the response. Oxfam&apos;s response is partner led, and Oxfam will work with1 national partner in Gazafor the implementation of this project.

Currently, Oxfam is using the following supply lines:
- Egypt: WASH (latrines, bladders, tanks, handwashing stations, hygiene kits), protection and shelter items; ECHO flight shipments from Oxfam&#x2019;s UK Supply Centre to El Arish airport; Food kits and hygiene items procured in Egypt; MOU with IOMfor transportation. Currently, Oxfam is looking for other options beyond IOM to support on both procurement and transportation to Gaza via Karam Shalom.
- Jordan: Food kits, WASH items, hygiene items, dignity items procured in Jordan; International ECHOflight shipments to Amman for other WASH items; coordination with Logistics cluster and JCHO for cargo movement. Currently, Oxfam is looking for other options beyond Logs cluster and JCHO to support on cargo movement to Gaza via Erez and Karam Shalom.
-West Bank: Food and hygiene items: Oxfam is exploring this route in addition to the above options, to support the local Palestinian vendors/market</narrative>
  </description>
